# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
# Permutation 4 of the Grafana Cloud kubernetes-monitoring configuration docs
# (config-other-methods/otel-collector-receivers): a DaemonSet running otlp, hostmetrics and
# filelog, plus a Deployment running otlp, k8s_cluster and k8sobjects. This is a different
# metric NAMESPACE, not a transport change, and it is the deployment SKT-0007.01 cited when it
# verdicted k8s_cluster and host OTEL-NATIVE.
#
# CAPTURE STATUS IS UNPROVEN. This harness can select and deploy the permutation; curating its
# capture into the corpus, resolving cantfind SK-85 from the kubeletstats default-enabled set,
# and recording its observable differences in signals/ is SKT-0013.01's work, not this one's.
PERMUTATION_TITLE="OTel Collector native receivers (DaemonSet hostmetrics/filelog + Deployment k8s_cluster/k8sobjects)"
PERMUTATION_SUMMARY="A genuinely different metric namespace: OTel-native receivers rather than Prometheus-shaped scrapes."
PERMUTATION_COLLECTOR="open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector"
PERMUTATION_COLLECTOR_VERSION="0.171.0"
PERMUTATION_CORPUS_AREAS="k8s host otlp-metrics"
PERMUTATION_CAPTURE_STATUS="unproven"
PERMUTATION_DEVIATIONS="The documented otlphttp exporter authenticates to Grafana Cloud with a basicauth extension; the lab has no credential, so the exporter targets the in-cluster capture receiver with no auth and skips verification of a throw-away self-signed certificate.|k8s.cluster.name is set to the lab cluster label rather than the operator's cluster name.|Everything else — receivers, processors, presets and pipelines — is the documented configuration verbatim, because the point of the capture is the shape it produces."
